Hi all,

After removing Ira's IPP talk and Piotr's OAuth session we remain with:

> 
>    - CUPS 2.5/3.x - Michael Sweet
>    - Immutable distros, packaging - Till Kamppeter
>    - Desktop Integration - Till Kamppeter
>    - General Q & A - Till Kamppeter
> 

And as we did not really plan actual new features but just are on the 
way to implement all of them, I am thinking about renaming the series 
just into "OpenPrinting" (no "Roadmap Sprint") with the principal idea 
to show the students in Mandi what OpenPrinting is doing and where 
volunteers are needed.

Zdenek, I want to ask you whether you would also attend our OpenPrinting 
track (remotely). Also would be nice if you could give a talk/host a 
session, about anything Red-Hat-related with printing.

Zdenek, independent if you present something or just only attend, I will 
connect you so that you can talk live in the discussions.

Zdenek, with Mike and you on the virtual stage and me in the room we 
have at least the core team of OpenPrinting in the session. There will 
also some of the GSoC contributors/mentors from Mandi, and depending on 
how we finally schedule, also Aveek, also perhaps Ira, depending how 
quickly his commitments end on that day.

So the students in Mandi will meet the team and I hope they get 
attracted to join OPenPrinting.

By the way, even if not actually a Roadmap Sprint any more, everything 
will get streamed live and not only the in-person audience can ask 
questions but also anyone watching us on YouTube or Twitch can type 
questions.

    Till
